# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project documentation is NOT committed.
#
# The SRS, POC scope and agreement, project brief, axle reference and capture
# sheet analysis are the specification. They live in Confluence, which is where
# the sponsor reads and comments on them, and they change on a different clock
# from the code. A copy in git would immediately become a stale second
# authority — the exact failure the project brief exists to prevent.
#
# `docs/spec/` may hold a local untracked mirror for offline work and for
# grepping. It is a cache, never the source. `.mcp.json` ships the Atlassian
# server so a session in this repo can read Confluence directly.
#
# What IS committed: ADRs, architecture, runbooks, CONTRIBUTING — documentation
# ABOUT the repository, which belongs beside the code it describes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/spec/
docs/prototypes/

# Machine-generated seeds. Regenerate with `make db-seeds` — the generators are
# the single source of truth for the axle configuration library, and committing
# 184KB of near-identical INSERTs helps nobody.
db/seeds/002_seed_configurations.sql
db/seeds/003_seed_fixture.sql

node_modules/
dist/

# Playwright run artefacts: traces and reports are per-run diagnostics (CI
# uploads them on failure), never source.
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
api/bin/
# `go build ./...` drops the main-package binary here
/api/api
/api/api.exe
coverage/
.vite/
